<TITLE>Jet Pump</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "ORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>In the saddle type tank, when the remaining fuel becomes low, the tank is divided into 2 chambers, A and B, and fuel remains in chamber B. The jet pump uses the flow velocity of the return fuel in the fuel tank to draw up fuel by the vacuum generated when it passes through the venturi, transferring fuel from chamber B to chamber A.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
